          question: 'How does ClickMasters handle Australian data residency requirements?',
          answer: 'Australian data residency requirements vary by industry and data type. Federal government data (Protected and higher): must be hosted in Australia on a Hosting Certification Framework (HCF) certified provider  ClickMasters deploys government workloads on AWS ap-southeast-2 (Sydney) with the appropriate IRAP (Information Security Registered Assessors Programme) assessment. Healthcare data (My Health Records Act): must be stored and processed within Australia  ClickMasters deploys healthcare workloads in AWS ap-southeast-2 with Australian-specific security controls. State health data: NSW Health, Victorian Department of Health, and most state health agencies require data to remain within Australia  ClickMasters implements data residency controls as standard for health sector clients. Financial services data (APRA guidance): APRA expects regulated entities to maintain oversight of outsourced data and be able to retrieve data from offshore providers  ClickMasters documents data flows and provides Australian data residency as the default for APRA-regulated client engagements. For clients without mandatory data residency requirements, ClickMasters defaults to AWS ap-southeast-2 (Sydney) for the best performance for Australian users.',
