          question: 'What is SR&ED and can ClickMasters engagements qualify?',
          answer: 'SR&ED (Scientific Research and Experimental Development) is a Canadian federal tax incentive program that provides income tax credits for eligible R&D expenditures. Canadian companies can claim up to 35% of eligible expenditures (for Canadian Controlled Private Corporations) or 15% (for other corporations) as refundable or non-refundable tax credits. ClickMasters engagements that involve eligible experimental development work (technological advancement through systematic investigation or experimentation to achieve a result that is not deterministic from existing knowledge) may qualify for SR&ED. ClickMasters provides technical documentation describing the experimental development activities, the technological uncertainty, and the technical advancement achieved  the documentation that SR&ED claims require. Canadian clients should engage an SR&ED specialist (many Canadian accounting firms have dedicated SR&ED teams) to assess whether a specific ClickMasters engagement qualifies.',
